      "searchable": "build a data lake with autonomous ai lakehouse 11351 3689 adb serverless lauran.serhal@oracle.com workshop quarterly qa complete workshop level intermediate github repository adb repository mapping status mapped from current wms livelabs id 3689 wms id 11351 wms workshop title build a data lake with oracle autonomous ai lakehouse content type workshop publish status published publish type public workshop status quarterly qa complete council area adb serverless wms last update 3/13/2026 completion date 5/15/2023 author coverage individual author contact coverage tier individual workshop time 2.5 views - last 7 days 17309 views - last 14 days 6522 views - last 30 days 17304 views - last 90 days 29235 views - last 180 days 45679 views - last 12 months 57263 workshop level intermediate github repository adb repository mapping status mapped from current wms repository mapping evidence github_pages update evidence live github workshop path (high confidence) update confidence high update scope workshop-specific git evidence latest github update 2026-03-20 last meaningful workshop update 2026-03-20 latest workshop commit date 2026-03-20 first workshop commit date 2022-06-20 latest live repo commit date 2026-03-20 latest workshop markdown commit date 2026-03-20 latest meaningful commit build a data lake with oracle autonomous ai lakehouse (hol events cha… git commit author lauranserhal resolved workshop path shared/adw-data-lake/build-data-lake/workshops/freetier resolved manifest path shared/adw-data-lake/build-data-lake/workshops/freetier/manifest.json acknowledgement date 2026-03-01 acknowledgement author lauran k. serhal, consulting user assistance developer, oracle autonomous ai database and multicloud acknowledgement updater lauran k. serhal acknowledgement source file shared/adw-data-lake/build-data-lake/introduction/introduction.md acknowledgement vs git matches git month acknowledgement vs wms wms workshop update n/a publish type resolution confirmed from current or stable id history publish type resolution reason publish type is present in the reconciled wms record. livelabs id 3689 wms id 11351 wms workshop title build a data lake with oracle autonomous ai lakehouse content type workshop publish status published publish type public workshop status quarterly qa complete council area adb serverless wms last update 3/13/2026 completion date 5/15/2023 author coverage individual author contact coverage tier individual workshop time 2.5 production url https://livelabs.oracle.com/ords/dbpm/r/livelabs/view-workshop?wid=3689 production github url https://oracle-livelabs.github.io/adb/shared/adw-data-lake/build-data-lake/workshops/freetier/index.html owner email lauran.serhal@oracle.com owner group db product management short description with oracle autonomous ai lakehouse, customers can build data lakes from scratch or by augmenting existing data warehouse implementations. data lakes help customers who want to maximize business output from their data capital. oracle proudly offers a wide range of database features to help customers to implement the all-data strategy. long description data is everywhere stored both locally and on the cloud in different format such as csv, parquet, json, orc, avro, and the new table format that will be available soon such as iceberg and delta share. although the metadata can stored in different places, autonomous ai lakehouse can work with it whether it is stored locally (using pl/sql,api, and the ui) or in central places in data catalogs (such as oci dcat and aws glue). ai lakehouse provides high performance when querying external data at scale. finally, ai lakehouse provides multi-language support to process data lakes such as sql, python, r, and rest. the labs in this workshop walk you through all the steps that you need to build and access the data lake (oracle object storage buckets) using autonomous ai lakehouse. first, you set-up the workshop environment and create the necessary resources such as a compartment, an autonomous ai lakehouse instance, and oracle object storage resources. next, evolve object storage files into meaningful business entities by defining the metadata for external data in ai lakehouse using several methods such as programmatically using pl/sql scripts, using the database actions user interface, or by synchronizing with data catalogs (to derive the metadata) such as oci data catalog and aws glue. next, you can gain insights from data lakes by querying data that lives in your oracle ai lakehouse and combine that with data that is stored in your oracle object storage buckets using regular sql select statements that includes joined tables. you also move data to object storage buckets by exporting your datasets. finally, you query your data using the sql worksheet. views - last 7 days 17309 views - last 7 days rank 10 views - last 14 days 6522 views - last 14 days rank 9 views - last 30 days 17304 views - last 30 days rank 10 views - last 90 days 29235 views - last 90 days rank 10 views - last 180 days 45679 views - last 180 days rank 6 views - last 12 months 57263 views - last 12 months rank 10 dashboard metric status available_unique_title_scope dashboard metric scope exact_unique_title dashboard metric resolution dashboard metrics matched one current wms title. dashboard shared record count 1 focus ai services - ai/machine learning, database - data warehouse/lakehouse, development - analytics, development - database, other - administration focus area ai services - ai/machine learning, database - data warehouse/lakehouse, development - analytics, development - database, other - administration product autonomous db serverless - autonomous ai database - serverless, cloud infrastructure (oci) - oci data catalog, cloud infrastructure (oci) - oci identity and access, database cloud service - autonomous ai database, database cloud service - autonomous ai lakehouse role administrator, application dev., business analyst, data scientist, developer, it administrator, power user"
