      "searchable": "oracle integration 3 - automate invoice processing with oci document understanding 11664 3979 oic - integration kishore.x.katta@oracle.com workshop quarterly qa complete workshop level beginner github repository oic repository mapping status mapped from current wms livelabs id 3979 wms id 11664 content type workshop publish status published publish type public workshop status quarterly qa complete council area oic - integration wms last update 9/10/2025 completion date 7/31/2025 author coverage individual author contact coverage tier individual workshop time 2.75 views - last 7 days 198 views - last 14 days 109 views - last 30 days 198 views - last 90 days 694 views - last 180 days 1200 views - last 12 months 2516 workshop level beginner github repository oic repository mapping status mapped from current wms repository mapping evidence github_pages update evidence live github workshop path (high confidence) update confidence high update scope workshop-specific git evidence latest github update 2026-04-03 last meaningful workshop update 2026-04-03 latest workshop commit date 2026-04-03 first workshop commit date 2022-09-07 latest live repo commit date 2026-04-03 latest workshop markdown commit date 2024-07-22 latest meaningful commit change github.io refs to cdn (#110) git commit author klazarz resolved workshop path opa-for-fusionapps/invoice-handling-process/workshops/tenancy resolved manifest path opa-for-fusionapps/invoice-handling-process/workshops/tenancy/manifest.json acknowledgement date 2024-06-01 acknowledgement author kishore katta, oracle integration product management acknowledgement updater kishore katta acknowledgement contributors harris qureshi (app integration specialist), stanislav tanev (opa product management) acknowledgement source file opa-for-fusionapps/invoice-handling-process/introduction/introduction.md acknowledgement vs git acknowledgement date trails latest git update by 51 days acknowledgement vs wms wms workshop update n/a publish type resolution confirmed from current or stable id history publish type resolution reason publish type is present in the reconciled wms record. livelabs id 3979 wms id 11664 content type workshop publish status published publish type public workshop status quarterly qa complete council area oic - integration wms last update 9/10/2025 completion date 7/31/2025 author coverage individual author contact coverage tier individual workshop time 2.75 production url https://livelabs.oracle.com/ords/dbpm/r/livelabs/view-workshop?wid=3979 production github url https://oracle-livelabs.github.io/oic/opa-for-fusionapps/invoice-handling-process/workshops/tenancy owner email kishore.x.katta@oracle.com owner group other product management short description in this live lab, we'll explore leveraging the oci ai services feature in opa to build an automated invoice processing orchestration workflow. this workflow will read invoice pdf documents, extract relevant data using ai powered document understanding service, validate the extracted information, and store it in a database. the workflow will notify the user if the extracted data is not approved. long description this tutorial will cover the following steps: 1. ingesting invoice pdf documents: we'll start by ingesting invoice pdf documents into the workflow. this will be done by the stakeholder uploading the document by launching a processing application web form. 2. extracting invoice data with oci document ai service: next, the workflow leverages oci's document ai service to extract key information from the invoice pdfs, such as invoice number, date, total amount, line items, and vendor details. this ai services document control leverages advanced machine learning models to understand the structure and layout of documents, enabling accurate data extraction. 3. validating extracted invoice data: after extracting the invoice data, we'll implement a validation process to ensure the integrity and completeness of the extracted information. this could involve checking for missing or inconsistent data 4. triggering oic integration flow for saving the invoices: if the extracted invoice data is deemed valid during the validation process, we'll trigger an oic integration flow. this integration flow will initiate a series of actions to save the invoice in the database. we will oic event system to publish the invoice details. 5. storing valid invoice data in a database: a subscriber integration flow will transform and persist the invoice details in a database for further processing or integration with other systems, such as accounting or enterprise resource planning (erp) systems. for this live lab we will consider the invoice records to be stored in a database. however, the design pattern can easily be extended to create another seamless subscriber integration flow and create an invoice record in erp cloud. throughout the live lab, we'll explore the usage of oci ai services- document understanding form control and extend the use case to invoke an integration flow to persist the invoice record in db. we will also explore opa analytics to identify the process trends, and errors, and understand how long processes take to complete and why. by the end of this live lab, you'll have a comprehensive understanding of how to build an end-to-end invoice processing integration using oci ai services, ensuring accurate data extraction, validation, and storage, while streamlining the processing of valid invoices through automated workflows. views - last 7 days 198 views - last 7 days rank 304 views - last 14 days 109 views - last 14 days rank 307 views - last 30 days 198 views - last 30 days rank 304 views - last 90 days 694 views - last 90 days rank 289 views - last 180 days 1200 views - last 180 days rank 316 views - last 12 months 2516 views - last 12 months rank 334 dashboard metric status available_unique_title_scope dashboard metric scope exact_unique_title dashboard metric resolution dashboard metrics matched one current wms title. dashboard shared record count 1 focus ai services - ai/machine learning, application integration - integration, process automation focus area ai services - ai/machine learning, application integration - integration, process automation product database cloud service - autonomous ai transaction processing, database cloud service - oci document understanding, oracle integration cloud (oic) - oci integration role business analyst, business user, developer, low code developer sales play ai services - ai/machine learning, application integration - integration, business analyst, business user, database cloud service - autonomous ai transaction processing, database cloud service - oci document understanding, developer, low code developer, oracle integration cloud (oic) - oci integration, process automation"
