      "searchable": "maximize aiops efficiency with oci gen ai agents 11889 4209 ai services nikhil.nv.verma@oracle.com workshop quarterly qa complete workshop level beginner github repository analytics-ai repository mapping status mapped from current wms livelabs id 4209 wms id 11889 content type workshop publish status published publish type public workshop status quarterly qa complete council area ai services wms last update 5/8/2026 completion date 7/22/2025 author coverage individual author contact coverage tier individual workshop time 3 views - last 7 days 501 views - last 14 days 138 views - last 30 days 501 views - last 90 days 706 views - last 180 days 776 views - last 12 months 780 workshop level beginner github repository analytics-ai repository mapping status mapped from current wms repository mapping evidence github_pages update evidence local git mirror workshop path (high confidence) update confidence high update scope workshop-specific git evidence latest github update 2025-07-02 last meaningful workshop update 2025-07-02 latest workshop commit date 2025-07-02 first workshop commit date 2024-10-25 latest workshop markdown commit date 2025-07-02 latest meaningful commit wms 11889: maximize aiops efficiency with oci gen ai agents (#409) git commit author nikhilnvverma resolved workshop path maximize-aiops-efficiency-genai-agents/workshops/tenancy resolved manifest path maximize-aiops-efficiency-genai-agents/workshops/tenancy/manifest.json publish type resolution confirmed from current or stable id history publish type resolution reason publish type is present in the reconciled wms record. livelabs id 4209 wms id 11889 content type workshop publish status published publish type public workshop status quarterly qa complete council area ai services wms last update 5/8/2026 completion date 7/22/2025 author coverage individual author contact coverage tier individual workshop time 3 production url https://livelabs.oracle.com/ords/dbpm/r/livelabs/view-workshop?wid=4209 production github url https://oracle-livelabs.github.io/analytics-ai/maximize-aiops-efficiency-genai-agents/workshops/tenancy/index.html owner email nikhil.nv.verma@oracle.com owner group oci product management short description aiops represents a transformative approach that utilizes artificial intelligence and machine learning technologies to enhance and automate various it operations processes. long description this workshop demonstrates how to utilize oracle cloud infrastructure (oci) generative ai agents to automate it operations. a common and impactful use case has been selected for this demonstration—remediation of high cpu and memory utilization alarms. in this scenario, the oci generative ai agent leverages a runbook retrieved via a retrieval-augmented generation (rag) tool to determine the appropriate remediation steps and trigger the necessary tools to resolve the issue. while this workshop highlights a specific use case, the approach is extensible. organizations can integrate oci generative ai agents with existing it service management (itsm) systems to identify various it operational issues and automatically execute relevant runbooks for resolution. key components and services used: oci autonomous database (23ai) is utilized as the rag database to store and retrieve operational runbooks. oci email delivery service is configured to send real-time notification emails to the it operations team once remediation tasks are successfully completed. oci monitoring is used to define and configure alarms for cpu and memory utilization, triggering alerts when usage exceeds 90%. a test compute instance was provisioned to simulate cpu and memory stress using synthetic load generation tools (e.g., stress-ng), thereby creating realistic alarm scenarios. oci agent development kit (adk) was employed to develop and deploy the generative ai agents. slack was integrated as the front-end interface, allowing it users to query system health (e.g., cpu or memory alarms) and authorize the ai agent to perform remediation actions according to the runbook instructions. this end-to-end setup showcases the potential of oci generative ai in streamlining it operations, reducing mean time to resolution (mttr), and enhancing operational efficiency through intelligent automation. views - last 7 days 501 views - last 7 days rank 202 views - last 14 days 138 views - last 14 days rank 276 views - last 30 days 501 views - last 30 days rank 202 views - last 90 days 706 views - last 90 days rank 287 views - last 180 days 776 views - last 180 days rank 396 views - last 12 months 780 views - last 12 months rank 569 dashboard metric status available_unique_title_scope dashboard metric scope exact_unique_title dashboard metric resolution dashboard metrics matched one current wms title. dashboard shared record count 1 focus ai services - ai/machine learning, cloud infrastructure (oci) focus area ai services - ai/machine learning, cloud infrastructure (oci) product ai services - ai vector search, cloud infrastructure (oci) - cloud infrastructure, cloud infrastructure (oci) - compute instances, cloud infrastructure (oci) - oci identity and access, database - python role devops engineer, it"
